<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves fell to 61.9 bln ringgit.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves fell to 61.9 bln ringgit.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves fell to 61.9 billion ringgit as at July 15 against 70.7 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities fell</p>
<p>to 96.82 billion ringgit from 100.99 billion two weeks</p>
<p>earlier.</p>
<p>(In bln ringgit)  July 15 1997    June 30 1997    July 15 1996</p>
<p>Reserves		 61.90	     70.71	     66.68</p>
<p>Assets		   96.82	    100.99	     95.72</p>
<p>Currency		 22.07	     21.95	     19.38</p>
<p>Govt paper		1.72		1.74		3.64</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
</text>
